# Module Setup Rules

## Directory Structure

Each new module should follow this structure:

```
src/module_name/
├── module_name.module.ts     # NestJS module definition
├── module_name.controller.ts # REST endpoints
├── module_name.service.ts    # Business logic
├── module_name.repository.ts # Database interactions
├── schema.ts                 # Drizzle schema definition
├── dto/                      # DTOs directory
│   ├── create.dto.ts         # Create DTOs
│   ├── update.dto.ts         # Update DTOs
│   ├── query.dto.ts          # Query DTOs
│   └── response.dto.ts       # Response DTOs
├── entities/                 # Entity definitions (if needed)
│   └── module_name.entity.ts
└── docs/                     # Swagger documentation
    └── module_name.docs.ts   # API documentation definitions
```

## File Purposes

### 1. Module (`module_name.module.ts`)

NestJS module that wires together controllers, services, and imports.

```typescript
import { Module } from "@nestjs/common";
import { AuthModule } from "@/auth/auth.module";
import DatabaseModule from "@/database/database.module";

import ModuleController from "./module.controller";
import ModuleService from "./module.service";
import ModuleRepository from "./module.repository";

@Module({
  imports: [AuthModule, DatabaseModule],
  controllers: [ModuleController],
  providers: [ModuleService, ModuleRepository],
  exports: [ModuleRepository],
})
export default class ModuleModule {}
```

### 2. Controller (`module_name.controller.ts`)

REST endpoints with Swagger decorators.

```typescript
import { Controller, Get, Post, Put, Delete, Param, Body, Query } from "@nestjs/common";
import { ApiTags, ApiOperation, ApiResponse } from "@nestjs/swagger";
import { ResponseWrapper, buildResponse } from "@/types";
import { ModuleService } from "./module.service";
import { CreateModuleDto, UpdateModuleDto } from "./dto";

@ApiTags("Modules")
@Controller("modules")
export class ModuleController {
  constructor(private readonly moduleService: ModuleService) {}

  @Get()
  @ApiOperation({ summary: "List all modules" })
  @ApiResponse({ status: 200, description: "Modules retrieved successfully" })
  async findAll(): Promise<ResponseWrapper<any[]>> {
    const data = await this.moduleService.findAll();
    return buildResponse({ data, code: "OK" });
  }
}
```

### 3. Service (`module_name.service.ts`)

Business logic layer.

```typescript
import { Injectable } from "@nestjs/common";
import { ModuleRepository } from "./module.repository";
import { CreateModuleDto, UpdateModuleDto } from "./dto";

@Injectable()
export class ModuleService {
  constructor(private readonly moduleRepository: ModuleRepository) {}

  async findAll() {
    return this.moduleRepository.findAll();
  }

  async create(createDto: CreateModuleDto) {
    return this.moduleRepository.create(createDto);
  }
}
```

### 4. Repository (`module_name.repository.ts`)

Database operations using Drizzle ORM.

```typescript
import { Injectable } from "@nestjs/common";
import { DatabaseService } from "@/database/database.service";
import { moduleTable } from "./schema";

@Injectable()
export class ModuleRepository {
  constructor(private readonly db: DatabaseService) {}

  async findAll() {
    return this.db.client.select().from(moduleTable);
  }

  async create(data: any) {
    const [result] = await this.db.client
      .insert(moduleTable)
      .values(data)
      .returning();
    return result;
  }
}
```

### 5. Schema (`schema.ts`)

Drizzle ORM table definitions.

```typescript
import { pgTable, serial, text, timestamp, boolean } from "drizzle-orm/pg-core";

export const moduleTable = pgTable("modules", {
  id: serial("id").primaryKey(),
  name: text("name").notNull(),
  description: text("description"),
  isActive: boolean("is_active").default(true),
  createdAt: timestamp("created_at").defaultNow(),
  updatedAt: timestamp("updated_at").defaultNow(),
});
```

### 6. DTOs (`dto/`)

Data Transfer Objects for validation and serialization.

#### Create DTO (`dto/create.dto.ts`)

```typescript
import { IsString, IsOptional } from "class-validator";

export class CreateModuleDto {
  @IsString()
  name: string;

  @IsOptional()
  @IsString()
  description?: string;
}
```

#### Update DTO (`dto/update.dto.ts`)

```typescript
import { IsString, IsOptional, IsBoolean } from "class-validator";
import { PartialType } from "@nestjs/mapped-types";
import { CreateModuleDto } from "./create.dto";

export class UpdateModuleDto extends PartialType(CreateModuleDto) {
  @IsOptional()
  @IsBoolean()
  isActive?: boolean;
}
```

#### Response DTO (`dto/response.dto.ts`)

```typescript
import { ApiProperty } from "@nestjs/swagger";

export class ModuleResponseDto {
  @ApiProperty()
  id: number;

  @ApiProperty()
  name: string;

  @ApiProperty({ required: false })
  description?: string;

  @ApiProperty()
  isActive: boolean;
}
```

### 7. Docs (`docs/module_name.docs.ts`)

Swagger documentation definitions.

```typescript
import { ApiProperty } from "@nestjs/swagger";
import { CreateModuleDto } from "../dto/create.dto";
import { ModuleResponseDto } from "../dto/response.dto";

export const CreateModuleApiBody = {
  type: CreateModuleDto,
  description: "Module creation data",
};

export const CreateModuleApiResponse = {
  status: 201,
  description: "Module created successfully",
  type: ModuleResponseDto,
};
```

## NestJS Patterns

### Dependency Injection

Use constructor injection for dependencies:

```typescript
constructor(
  private readonly moduleService: ModuleService,
  private readonly emailService: EmailService,
) {}
```

### Response Wrapper

Use the project's response wrapper pattern:

```typescript
import { ResponseWrapper, buildResponse, ResponseCode } from "@/types";

return buildResponse({
  data: result,
  code: ResponseCode.OK,
  message: "Operation successful",
});
```

### Validation

Use class-validator decorators for DTO validation:

```typescript
import { IsString, IsEmail, MinLength, IsOptional } from "class-validator";
```

### Database Transactions

Use transactions for complex operations:

```typescript
async createWithRelations(data: CreateModuleDto) {
  return this.db.transaction(async (tx) => {
    const module = await tx.insert(moduleTable).values(data).returning();
    // Additional operations in same transaction
    return module[0];
  });
}
```

## Authentication & Authorization

### Protected Routes

Use NestJS guards for authentication:

```typescript
import { UseGuards } from "@nestjs/common";
import { JwtAuthGuard } from "@/auth/guards/jwt-auth.guard";

@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)
@Post()
async create(@Body() createDto: CreateModuleDto) {
  // Protected endpoint
}
```

### User Context

Get current user from request:

```typescript
import { CurrentUser } from "@/auth/decorators/current-user.decorator";

@Post()
async create(
  @Body() createDto: CreateModuleDto,
  @CurrentUser() user: UserEntity,
) {
  // Use user context
}
```

## Testing Patterns

### Unit Tests

Test services and repositories in isolation:

```typescript
describe("ModuleService", () => {
  let service: ModuleService;
  let repository: jest.Mocked<ModuleRepository>;

  beforeEach(async () => {
    const module = await Test.createTestingModule({
      providers: [
        ModuleService,
        {
          provide: ModuleRepository,
          useValue: mockRepository,
        },
      ],
    }).compile();

    service = module.get<ModuleService>(ModuleService);
    repository = module.get(ModuleRepository);
  });
});
```

### E2E Tests

Test full request/response cycle:

```typescript
describe("ModuleController (e2e)", () => {
  let app: INestApplication;

  beforeEach(async () => {
    const moduleFixture = await Test.createTestingModule({
      imports: [AppModule],
    }).compile();

    app = moduleFixture.createNestApplication();
    await app.init();
  });
});
```

## Import Aliases

Use path aliases defined in `tsconfig.json`:

```typescript
import { ResponseWrapper } from "@/types";
import { DatabaseService } from "@/database/database.service";
import AuthModule from "@/auth/auth.module";
```

## Error Handling

Use NestJS built-in exceptions:

```typescript
import {
  NotFoundException,
  BadRequestException,
  ConflictException,
  UnauthorizedException,
} from "@nestjs/common";
```

## Logging

Use NestJS logger:

```typescript
import { Logger } from "@nestjs/common";

private readonly logger = new Logger(ModuleService.name);

this.logger.log("Creating new module");
this.logger.error("Failed to create module", error);
```

## Internationalization

Usenestjs-i18n for internationalization:

```typescript
import { I18n, I18nContext } from "nestjs-i18n";

constructor(private readonly i18n: I18nService) {}

async create(data: CreateModuleDto) {
  return this.i18n.t("module.created", {
    lang: I18nContext.current().lang,
  });
}
```
